{"ts":"2026-08-09T06:08:48.290Z","author":"harness:claude-code","author_source":"detected","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_model":"claude-opus-5","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"7585198bf575ad9621c321e3","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"claude-opus-5","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"environment"},"role":null,"topic":{"value":"pm-b84irw","source":"argv"},"version":{"value":"2.1.226","source":"probe"}},"op":"learning_add","patch":[{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-08-09T06:08:48.290Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/learnings","value":[{"created_at":"2026-08-09T06:08:48.290Z","author":"harness:claude-code","text":"Ask a gate what its denominator is, and who computes it. A gate whose input is a hand-written list of instances reports a pass rate of one by construction: it examines what someone enumerated, agrees with itself, and says nothing about the population it was built to police. The verdict is honest and the inference drawn from it is not.\n\nThe tell is that widening coverage and finding a defect are indistinguishable from outside — both show up as the list getting longer — so there is no signal that separates 'we are covering more' from 'there was more than we thought'. Three instruments in this repo had the shape simultaneously on 2026-08-09 (surface-replication-sets.json, smoke-external-packages.mjs, sdk/public-surface.json vs src/sdk/index.ts), which suggests the shape is a default a quality mechanism falls into rather than an oversight in any one of them.\n\nPractical form: before writing a gate, name the set it claims to speak for and check whether that set is computable from the tree. If it is, compute it and emit examined-over-total. If it is not, the gate is a regression test and should be described as one, never cited as coverage."}]}],"before_hash":"80b9af57993108289a89776fbd4ed857363b075fed0b5435f76c51afad2ad2ad","after_hash":"d5fbeb412511feb906a80e9933e392300c179e982a1267b1bbdeb